# SQL Rental Business Analysis
This project analyzes rental store performance using PostgreSQL queries built on the DVD rental dataset.
The analysis focuses on identifying revenue trends, pricing issues, inventory performance, and rental behavior across store locations.

## Skills Demonstrated
- Complex SQL joins
- Aggregations and grouping
- Business reporting queries
- User-defined SQL functions
- Triggers for automated summary updates
- Stored procedures for refreshing reporting tables

## Business Questions
Examples of questions answered in this project:
• Which film genres generate the most rentals?  
• Which titles generate the most revenue?  
• Are some films priced incorrectly relative to demand?  
• How do different store locations compare in revenue?

## Technologies
- PostgreSQL
- SQL
- Data aggregation
- ETL automation concepts
